      "writtenOn": "2024-02-23T16:28:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the CI log snippet (https://object-store.cloud.muni.cz/swift/v1/ci-logs-public/30/6930/8/check/czechlight-gammarus-dashboard/34c9396/job-output.txt):\n\n2024-02-22 12:55:31.329309 | w | 1 high severity vulnerability\n2024-02-22 12:55:31.329314 | w |\n2024-02-22 12:55:31.329318 | w | To address all issues, run:\n2024-02-22 12:55:31.329321 | w |   npm audit fix\n\nThat brings a few questions:\n\n1) How did this happen?\n2) How serious it is?\n3) How come that the build still passes if it\u0027s indeed a serious error?\n\n(In the real life, nobody reads the logs unless the CI says \"boo boo\".)",
      "revId": "0f4c298e9f9fb5b8e93ccad8256aff4523787496",
      "serverId": "e32f8df8-3db0-4f76-a6c6-fe9d6e69dd68"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c1434ff9_b4c8c41f",
